## Week 1 Baseline

**Date:** 2026-09-02 · **Commit:** f4e16e7 · **Model:** claude-sonnet-4-6 · **n=20**
Baseline: `results/run_20260902-2126.json` · Replicate (noise floor): `results/run_20260902-2209.json`

### The golden set
20 records, single expert annotator, synthetic but domain-realistic. Coverage:
every billing category ≥3 cases, 4 out-of-scope cases, 1 designated boundary
case, 1 contradiction probe. Every gold label carries an adjudication note
stating its decisive signal.

### Results

| Field | Accuracy |
|-------|---------:|
| Category | 95% (19/20) |
| Priority | 85% (17/20) |
| Routing  | 85% (17/20) |

**By category:** 5 of 6 categories at 100%; the single category miss is the
deliberate contradiction probe (EX-002), misread as a meter fault.

**Escalation safety:** 0 dangerous errors (out-of-scope filed as billing) and
0 over-escalations, across 4 out-of-scope records.

**Calibration:** "high" 100% (10/10), "medium" 87% (7/8) — no inversion;
"low" (2/2) too small to read.

**Noise floor:** two identical-spec runs differ by 1 record (5 points, priority
field, EX-019) — the bar any future change must clear.

**Cost:** $0.11 per 20-record run ≈ half a cent per triaged exception.

### What error analysis found
Every miss received a three-way verdict (gold wrong / spec weak / model wrong):

- **Gold wrong: 4 · Spec weak: 2 · Model wrong: 0.** The answer key had more
  errors than the model — a well-documented pattern in single-annotator
  datasets, and exactly the risk this README's limitations flagged.
- Three of the four label errors are the same error: an under-specified P2/P3
  priority boundary (EX-012, EX-017, EX-019) — which is also where the
  run-to-run instability lives (EX-019).
- Both spec-weak misses have named missing sentences (EX-002: bill-computation
  tiebreaker; EX-015: routing rule for P1 disconnection risk).

### Honest limitations
- n=20 is a smoke test: gross failures are meaningful; small differences are
  one record of noise.
- Single annotator — and the risk materialized: 4 of 6 miss-verdicts were
  annotation errors, now queued for correction.
- Synthetic data written by the annotator — realistic, but style-correlated.
- The "low" confidence bucket (n=2) and the cause-unidentifiable contradiction
  flavor remain effectively untested (golden-set expansion items).

