### Design decisions
[...]
- **Priority is defined by impact; routing by next action.** A
  routing-derived priority definition was proposed twice and rejected twice
  against the golden set's own labels: EX-001/006/010/012 are P2 with Field
  Service Order routing (kills "P2 = Billing Analyst involved"), and
  EX-004/008 are P1 with CSR Callback (kills "CSR = P3"). The correlation
  between the fields is real but has a common cause — the record's facts —
  so it survives as lint checks in the harness, never as definitions.
- **Unconfirmed money discrepancies are P2** (shop ruling, 2026-09-18). A
  member-reported discrepancy is treated as a money error in flight until
  verified, because an unverified discrepancy carries forward on the account
  and compounds — toward delinquency, disconnection, and added charges — so
  the member is financially affected from the moment it is reported. Encoded
  as a clarification after the general P2/P3 rule; EX-019, unstable across
  five prior runs, stabilized immediately under it.